# Documentation (PAP)

- Write docs in European Portuguese unless Pedro asks otherwise.
- Keep `CONTEXTO-PAP.md` as the source of truth for goals, scope, and decisions.
- Document architecture, tests, privacy/ethics, costs, limits, and future work.
- Prefer short checklists and tables over long prose.
- Record hardware reuse inventory and justify new purchases.
- For LLM study: comparison table (quality, latency, privacy, hardware fit).
- Align claims with real MVP status — no fake “done” features.
- Per-file code explanations live in `docs/codigo/` (index: `README.md`). Keep them updated with the code.
